# KIND Cluster Setup Guide

## 1. Installing KIND and kubectl
wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LondheShubham153/kubestarter/main/kind-cluster/install.sh
ls -l install.sh
chmod +x install.sh
./install.sh


## 2. Setting Up the KIND Cluster
Create a config.yaml file:

kind: Cluster
apiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4
nodes:
  - role: control-plane
    image: kindest/node:v1.35.1
  - role: worker
    image: kindest/node:v1.35.1
  - role: worker
    image: kindest/node:v1.35.1
  - role: worker
    image: kindest/node:v1.35.1

## Create the cluster using the configuration file:
kind create cluster --config config.yaml --name my-cluster

## Verify the cluster:
kubectl get nodes
kubectl cluster-info

## 3. Accessing the Cluster
Use kubectl to interact with the cluster:
kubectl cluster-info

## 4. Setting Up the Kubernetes Dashboard
Deploy the Dashboard
##Apply the Kubernetes Dashboard manifest:
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/dashboard/v2.7.0/aio/deploy/recommended.yaml

## Create an Admin User
## Create a dashboard-admin-user.yml file with the following content:
nano dashboard-admin-user.yml

apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: admin-user
  namespace: kubernetes-dashboard

---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRoleBinding
metadata:
  name: admin-user
roleRef:
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
  kind: ClusterRole
  name: cluster-admin
subjects:
- kind: ServiceAccount
  name: admin-user
  namespace: kubernetes-dashboard

## Apply the configuration:
kubectl apply -f dashboard-admin-user.yml

##Verify ServiceAccount
kubectl get serviceaccount -n kubernetes-dashboard

## Generate the Dashboard Token
Retrieve the token for the admin-user
kubectl -n kubernetes-dashboard create token admin-user

## Copy the token for use in the Dashboard login.

## Access the Dashboard
## Start the Dashboard using kubectl proxy:
kubectl proxy

Keep this terminal running.

## Open the Dashboard in your browser:
http://localhost:8001/api/v1/namespaces/kubernetes-dashboard/services/https:kubernetes-dashboard:/proxy/

Use the token from the previous step to log in.

## 5. Deleting the Cluster
Delete the KIND cluster:
kind delete cluster --name my-cluster
